 ### Grid Traversal (Two-Pass)
-A two-pass algorithm to traverse voxel grids along rays, first counting segments to allocate exact memory, then filling them [S1, unofficial]. First pass: Call `traverse_grids_kernel` with `compute_intervals=true` (implied by first pass logic) and allocate `intervals.chunk_cnts` and `samples.chunk_cnts` tensors of size `[n_rays]` [S1, unofficial]. Second pass: Allocate data buffers for intervals and samples based on the counts from the first pass using `memalloc_data_from_chunk` [S1, unofficial]. Choose this when memory is constrained and the average number of steps per ray is significantly lower than the maximum, avoiding the waste of over-allocation.
